        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_019d005a70a0408a9244883369fefc46",
      "statement": "A memory sample obtains four measurements in one sampling turn: process RSS, in_use_bytes (RSS minus allocator slack), the cgroup working set (memory.current less inactive_file), and the complete cgroup current charge.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/memory.rs#L22-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:65223537a1c530547412cb7ab88cd5908afeb9579f5b07195525f2c188a9a861:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7995c11fa245457ab509e1db78a3f216",
      "statement": "in_use_bytes is RSS minus the pages jemalloc keeps but nothing uses, computed from stats.resident less stats.allocated after advancing the allocator epoch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/memory.rs#L164-L178",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1bf3a3c0239a48af838cec2ccf071d30145faab234262bddd9ec7d5b3ae19485:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_26fddefd3229487099e4b3290f9b6e6b",
      "statement": "On a readable Linux memory cgroup, the working set is memory.current less the inactive_file charge from memory.stat, which includes active kernel charges that process RSS does not report and excludes file and allocator pages.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/memory.rs#L39-L99",
